depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":15,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The judge stage for CAT-02 passed with no defects. The verdict is in `tasks/CAT-02/judge.md`.\n\nCAT-02 is an adopted story, so nothing was built. The only question was whether each mapped test proves its scenario. I checked each test against its scenario's `Given` / `When` / `Then` / `And`, using the scenario's own values. All five are met:\n\n- **View Details opens the product page:** the Playwright test clicks the card titled \"Domain-Driven Design\" and asserts the page's heading.\n- **Image, description, category:** the integration test checks the image path and alt text, that the image is actually served, the exact description, and \"Category\" = \"Books\".\n- **Tab title:** the page title is \"Clean Architecture\".\n- **Breadcrumb:** it reads \"Home / Products / Clean Architecture\", and the two links go to `/` and `/products`.\n- **Back to Products:** following the link from \"Team Topologies\" opens \"Our Products\".\n\nThings I noted but didn't count as defects:\n- **Browser break not run:** the patch meant to make the browser test fail was never run. I checked it by reasoning instead. The catalogue sorts by name, so the first card is the \"Domain over Framework\" hoodie, not \"Domain-Driven Design\", and the heading check would fail. Whether the patch applies and turns the test red is left to the gate. The four integration test breaks were already shown to fail in the test stage.\n- **Shared-scenario title:** the browser test's title \"View Details on a catalogue card opens that product's page\" still has to be added to the specification's `scenarios.md`, and the Java suite needs a test with the same title. That's your decision, and the test stage already flagged it.\n- **Other stories' changes in the diff:** the catalogue title change in `Catalog.cshtml`, the new E2E test harness files, and the AGENTS.md/README edits belong to `catalogue-title`, CAT-01 and the E2E harness change, which share this working tree. I didn't review them. None of the CAT-02 tests depend on them.\n\nI didn't run the ddd, hexagonal or dca reviews because adopt mode has no production code to review. I didn't change any code or run any other stage.","ttft_ms":4370,"type":"result","duration_ms":117589,"uuid":"6e0b193b-c482-427e-a16c-df63233528ea","ttft_stream_ms":3102,"time_to_request_ms":38,"first_content_frame_ms":3102,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
